    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "If DNA Digivolving, you choose 1 of your opponent's Digimon and return all of your opponent's Digimon with the same level to the bottom of the deck.  For example, if you use this effect to choose a level 3 Digimon, you return all of your opponent's level 3 Digimon to the bottom of the deck.  Then, you delete 1 of your opponent's Digimon.",
        "question": "What does this card's [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect do, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you may still delete one of the opponent's Digimon.",
        "question": "If this card didn’t DNA digivolve, can its [On Play] / [When Digivolving] effect still delete one of the opponent’s Digimon?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
